Usage: deq export [<shape...>] [options]

Export shapes in several formats and sizes.

Arguments:
  [<shape...>]  Shape ids; or use --all.

Options:
      --all                     Export every shape in the catalog.
      --format <list>           Comma-separated formats. Default svg. Values:
                                svg, svg-layered, svg-sprite, html, jsx, tsx,
                                vue, svelte, data-uri, css-background, css-mask,
                                pdf, ai, eps, png, jpg, webp, avif, ico,
                                favicon, psd, figma, spec-json.
      --sizes <list>            Comma-separated sizes in px. Default 24.
      --out <dir>               Output directory; files go to
                                <dir>/<format>/<size>/. Default the current
                                directory.
      --color <color>           Stroke and dot colour (any CSS colour). Default
                                currentColor.
      --stroke-width <n>        Stroke width in grid units, 0.05 to 12. Default
                                2.
      --absolute-stroke-width   Keep the stroke the same width in px at any
                                size.
      --fill <color>            Fill for closed outlines, or none. Default none.
      --fill-opacity <0-1>      Opacity of the fill. Default 1.
      --stroke-opacity <0-1>    Opacity of strokes and dots. Default 1.
      --linecap <linecap>       Line ends. Default round. Values: round, butt,
                                square.
      --linejoin <linejoin>     Line corners. Default round. Values: round,
                                miter, bevel.
      --dot-scale <n>           Multiply every dot radius, 0.1 to 4. Default 1.
      --rotation <deg>          Rotate clockwise about the centre. Default 0.
      --flip-x                  Mirror left to right.
      --flip-y                  Mirror top to bottom.
      --padding <n>             Space around the 24 x 24 canvas in grid units, 0
                                to 24. Default 0.
      --background <color>      Background colour, or none. Default none.
      --layer-color <layer=color>
                                Colour of one layer, for example sun=#FEBD11
                                (repeatable).
      --title <text>            Accessible title. Default the English name; ""
                                marks the image decorative.
      --param <name=value>      Shape parameter, for example rays=9 (repeatable;
                                see deq info).
      --current-color <color>   What currentColor means in PDF and image
                                formats. Default black.
      --matte <color>           JPG background behind transparent pixels.
                                Default white.
      --quality <0-100>         JPG and WebP quality. Default 90.
      --force                   Overwrite existing files.
  -h, --help                    Show help.
  -V, --version                 Print the version.
